{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And I will hear, for I am gracious.</b> Even though he cannot cry out against you for robbery, since after all he owes you — nevertheless, when <b>he cries out to Me</b> regarding his poverty, which causes him to be naked without clothing through your doing, I will grant him some of what I would have granted you beyond your sufficiency, so that you may thereby sustain others." "<b>For I am gracious.</b> And I bestow grace upon every suppliant who has none to show him grace but Me. Therefore it is good for you to show him grace by returning the pledge, so that grace from Me abides with you continually, and you are able to lend and to sustain others."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:48.582957015Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}